<p>Keap, formerly known as Infusionsoft, has been a mainstay in the small business automation space for years. It built its reputation on powerful, logic-driven automation workflows that gave business owners the ability to create sophisticated follow-up sequences and sales pipelines. If you have ever looked into <a href="/blog/marketing-automation-getting-started">marketing automation</a>, Keap has almost certainly come up in your research.</p>

<p>But Keap also built a reputation for something else: complexity. The platform that once made automation accessible to smaller teams has grown into a tool that many small business owners find difficult to learn, expensive to maintain, and hard to use without outside help.</p>

<p>So how does DUSA compare? Both platforms promise automation and CRM for growing businesses. The difference is in how they deliver on that promise, and what it costs to get there.</p>

<div class="divider">...</div>

<h2>What Keap does well</h2>

<p>Keap deserves credit for its automation engine. The campaign builder allows for deep branching logic, conditional triggers, and multi-step sequences that can handle deeply complex sales processes. If you need to build a workflow where different actions fire depending on which email a contact opened, which page they visited, and how they scored against your lead criteria, Keap can do that.</p>

<p>The platform also offers solid <a href="/blog/crm-small-business">CRM functionality</a>, invoice and payment processing, and appointment booking. For businesses that have invested the time to learn the system, Keap can become a central hub for managing contacts and sales.</p>

<p>That investment of time, however, is where the conversation gets more complicated.</p>

<h2>Where Keap gets complicated for small business</h2>

<p>Keap's pricing starts at $249 USD per month for the base plan. That is a significant commitment for a sole operator or small team, and the cost scales upward as you add contacts and users. For many small businesses, that price point alone puts Keap out of reach before they even evaluate the features.</p>

<p>Then there is the learning curve. Keap's automation builder, while powerful, is not intuitive. The campaign builder uses a visual drag-and-drop interface that looks approachable at first glance, but building effective workflows requires a solid understanding of tags, sequences, goals, and decision diamonds. Many users end up hiring a certified Keap consultant just to get their first campaigns configured properly.</p>

<blockquote><p>A tool that requires a consultant to set up is a tool built for companies with consultant budgets.</p></blockquote>

<p>There are also notable gaps in the feature set. Keap does not include a native funnel builder, which means you need a separate tool for landing pages and sales funnels. Review management is similarly absent, so collecting and managing customer reviews requires yet another integration or platform. For small business owners trying to consolidate their tools, those gaps matter.</p>

<h2>Where DUSA takes a different approach</h2>

<p>DUSA was designed for small business owners who want the benefits of automation without the steep learning curve or the enterprise price tag. Everything is included in one plan. CRM, email marketing, SMS, funnel builder, appointment booking, review management, automation, and pipeline management. There is no feature gating behind higher tiers.</p>

<p>The automation capabilities in DUSA are built for the workflows most small businesses actually need. Automated <a href="/blog/customer-follow-up-system">customer follow-up sequences</a>, appointment reminders, review requests after service, lead nurturing campaigns, and pipeline-triggered actions. You can build multi-step workflows without needing to understand complex branching logic or tag-based decision trees.</p>

<p>That does not mean DUSA is limited. It means the platform is designed so that the person running the business can also be the person setting up the automation, without weeks of training or outside help.</p>

